            "Provide a specific, developed example illustrating targeted practice's advantage — for instance, a musician who repeatedly plays a piece start-to-finish will likely reinforce the same recurring error in one difficult passage, while a musician who isolates and specifically drills that one passage addresses the actual weak point directly, producing faster improvement per hour invested.",
